From: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nbd: do not tear down sockets when NBD_DO_IT is interrupted
 by SIGSTOP

`nbd_start_device_ioctl` (the kernel-side body of `NBD_DO_IT`) waits
for all receive threads to finish via `wait_event_interruptible`. That
returns -ERESTARTSYS for *any* signal that wakes the task — including
SIGSTOP, which cannot be ignored by userspace.

systemd's `broadcast_signal()` in `src/shared/killall.c` does, in
sequence, `kill(-1, SIGSTOP)` → `killall(SIGTERM, …)` → `kill(-1,
SIGCONT)` when handling MANAGER_SWITCH_ROOT and MANAGER_SOFT_REBOOT.
The SIGSTOP half of that briefly stops every userspace process,
including a userspace `nbd-client` that is sitting in `NBD_DO_IT`.

When `wait_event_interruptible` wakes due to that SIGSTOP, the very
next lines of `nbd_start_device_ioctl` call `sock_shutdown(nbd)` and
`nbd_clear_que(nbd)`, *unconditionally* tearing down the NBD socket
and erroring out every in-flight request. The connection is now dead,
and any rootfs that lives on this nbd device EIOs immediately — even
though the userspace nbd-client was perfectly healthy, was woken up
by SIGCONT a moment later, would happily have ignored the SIGTERM via
its installed handler / SIG_IGN disposition, and would have continued
servicing requests.

For NBD-as-rootfs setups under systemd-in-initrd, this makes
`switch-root` impossible: the kernel tears down the rootfs NBD just
before systemd execs `/sbin/init` from /sysroot, and the exec fails
("No /sbin/init, trying fallback shell").

Switch the wait to `wait_event_killable`. That still allows SIGKILL
to break out of the ioctl (which is what userspace needs to actually
shut nbd-client down cleanly), but ignores transient stop/cont and
catchable-but-handled signals — exactly matching the semantics the
caller actually wants. SIGTERM with a userspace handler still gets
delivered when the task returns to userspace; the userspace handler
decides whether to call NBD_DISCONNECT explicitly.

Reproducer: any `nbd-client -n /dev/nbd0 …` running under a systemd
service through a `systemctl switch-root` transition.

Signed-off-by: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
---
 drivers/block/nbd.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/nbd.c b/drivers/block/nbd.c
--- a/drivers/block/nbd.c
+++ b/drivers/block/nbd.c
@@ -1552,8 +1552,8 @@ static int nbd_start_device_ioctl(struct nbd_device *nbd)
 	if (max_part)
 		set_bit(GD_NEED_PART_SCAN, &nbd->disk->state);
 	mutex_unlock(&nbd->config_lock);
-	ret = wait_event_interruptible(config->recv_wq,
-					 atomic_read(&config->recv_threads) == 0);
+	ret = wait_event_killable(config->recv_wq,
+					  atomic_read(&config->recv_threads) == 0);
 	if (ret) {
 		sock_shutdown(nbd);
 		nbd_clear_que(nbd);
